    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Home Prices Are Dipping. Is Now a Good Time to Buy?\"\nsubtitle: \"Prices are down a little. Mortgage rates are up a lot. Here's what that does to the monthly payment.\"\nauthor: \"SixtyEight95\"\ndate: \"2026-11-22\"\ncategories: [housing, cost of living, interest rates]\nimage: infographic.png\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\nYou may have seen headlines that home prices are finally coming down. Some are. So is this the moment to buy?\nWe pulled the latest market data to see what's actually changed for buyers, and what it does to the monthly payment.\n(This is general information, not financial advice; everyone's situation is different.)\n\n## The short answer\n\n::: {.callout-note appearance=\"simple\"}\nThe median listed home is **-2.2%** cheaper than a year ago. But mortgage rates rose from about\n**6.25%** to **7.33%**, so the monthly payment on that typical home is **$215 higher**:\nabout **$2,568 a month**, versus $2,353 a year ago.\n\nThe real change is leverage: more homes for sale, fewer buyers, and more room to negotiate than in years.\n:::\n\n## The monthly payment\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"plotly html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-3b0f03d328ee6f0d9104\" style=\"width:100%;height:417px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-3b0f03d328ee6f0d9104\">{\"x\":{\"data\":[{\"x\":[17167,17198,17226,17257,17287,17318,17348,17379,17410,17440,17471,17501,17532,17563,17591,17622,17652,17683,17713,17744,17775,17805,17836,17866,17897,17928,17956,17987,18017,18048,18078,18109,18140,18170,18201,18231,18262,18293,18322,18353,18383,18414,18444,18475,18506,18536,18567,18597,18628,18659,18687,18718,18748,18779,18809,18840,18871,18901,18932,18962,18993,19024,19052,19083,19113,19144,19174,19205,19236,19266,19297,19327,19358,19389,19417,19448,19478,19509,19539,19570,19601,19631,19662,19692,19723,19754,19783,19814,19844,19875,19905,19936,19967,19997,20028,20058,20